  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">23-0002387_Carrefours des Opportunites</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">23-0002387_The CarrOpps seeks to establish physical and digital multi-purpose hubs at community level, run by and for youth. with the aim to facilitate the positive engagement of male and female youths through their social and economic integration. Specifically, it seeks to increase Burkina Faso&#x2019;s rural communities capacity to provide livelihood &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; skills training to youth; increase male and female youth entrepreneurial skills, self-confidence and income generating opportunities; increase usage of digital tools and resources by young; Increase young entrepreneurs access to financial services and strengthen local community networks through G50 groups and UMVA platform.  In a 5-year period, CarrOpps aims to: - Establish 560 Hubs (60 physical + 500 G50) in 50 Communes - Provide in-person and digital economic and non-economic services to 75 ,000 youth - Served 50% female among targeted youth - Create, maintain, and improve 25,000 jobs - leverage &#x20ac;1,000,000 to support youth projects</narrative>
  </description>
